      "spec_id": "mip_frames_noactivation",
      "promise": "How do answer-form matching and rubric correctness compare after one missing-needs retrieval pass?",
      "matched": true,
      "caption": "FRAMES answer endpoints on 190 previously examined questions. Linked-passage retrieval uses a 50-piece head and a one-hop link witness, with activation off and merged-section delivery. Both arms receive 8000 initial tokens, the same steps instruction and at most one triggered retrieval of 4000 new tokens for reader-declared missing needs. RAG uses MMR relevance coefficient 0.7 over 200 candidates. Its relevance score is s + 0.4 h/max(h), where s is cosine plus 0.2 normalised BM25 and h is the dense seed. Pass-2 missing-need ranking adds 0.5 times the question score to the phrase score. The containment proxy counts exact matches or normalised substring/first-clause matches or token-F1 at least 0.5, with a three-times-reference length guard on the proxy. Judged correctness uses the banked majority rubric. The judged discordances are seven linked-passage-only successes and six RAG-only successes. Page presence and answer-bearing passage delivery are distinct, particularly for tables omitted from the plaintext corpus.",
